Oh

45
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,560
as a foreign patch...

46
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:08,920
The dream in the beginning...

47
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,100
There's no time,

48
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:12,920
Chapter 7 in the present,

49
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:17,420
The zero fades on its path.

50
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:25,060
Your front seat reaches the distance which lets around.

51
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:30,140
It inspires give you a series of wild facts.

52
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:40,180
My sincere apologies, Lord Plonkane. I am sorry to involve you.

53
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:43,140
Not at all. Your safety is part of my mission.

54
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,460
Your mission?

55
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:49,420
Yes. My orders to come here were received from his majesty himself.

56
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,140
Grandfather sent you?

57
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,160
The Emperor felt great concern.

58
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:59,180
Misgivings over conquering the Earth's system following the death of Count Sosbom.

59
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:05,580
So I was ordered to study the situation, and to personally ensure your safety.

60
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,760
It's imperative I speak to my grandfather at once.

61
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:15,180
It is possible to make contact. However...

62
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:18,780
Lord Plonkane, a transmission from the moon base.

63
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:20,040
Put it through.

64
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:25,740
My Lord Plonkane, may I ask where you are taking Princess of Salem?

65
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:31,540
My dear Count Troiard, I am simply evacuating her to a place of safety.

66
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:36,780
The moon base is a fortified location. There is no place where her highness would be more safe.

67
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,660
And yet, a battle was taking place there.

68
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:45,100
You may rest assured, the enemy has already been eliminated. Please, return at once.

69
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:46,760
I will not go back to you there!

70
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:55,480
While on Earth, I watched birds as they flew.

71
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:57,560
Yes, your highness.

72
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:02,560
The Earth was recovering. The world of man and nature coexisting.

73
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:06,160
You were the one who was teaching that to me.

74
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,560
That humans and nature...

75
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:10,560
That Earth in verse...

76
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,440
Could live and prosper together!

77
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:17,260
Yes, you are correct.

78
00:05:18,260 --> 00:05:20,120
I was the one who said that.

79
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:23,440
Stygia's squadron has been dispatched to pursue them.

80
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,340
Seize that ship on sight.

81
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:26,960
I'm begging you, Slane.

82
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:30,100
If you care for me at all, stop this war.

83
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:33,840
Please, make peace with Earth.

84
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,480
Very well.

85
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,820
Perhaps you're right.

86
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,820
Why don't you come back so that we can all discuss it?

87
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:44,020
Oh, Slane.

88
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,160
That sector is very dangerous.

89
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:48,680
Please return at once.

90
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:51,400
Lord Plonkane, you will turn back immediately.

91
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:52,780
I am afraid not.

92
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:56,620
I'm sorry, but I have orders from Princess Asalem.

93
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,640
Stealth mode to maximum, now!

94
00:05:58,880 --> 00:05:59,620
Yes, my lord.

95
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:05,140
Lord Plonkane's spaceship, the Hadriacus, has vanished.

96
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:07,760
Continue searching.

97
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:09,320
Yes, my lord.

98
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:12,540
For the time being, we won't have to worry about pursuit.

99
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,040
You have my gratitude.

100
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:19,140
Tell me, what am I to do now?

101
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:22,780
Well, Earth's military is pursuing me.

102
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:27,020
And all the orbital knights are backing Slane.

103
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:31,580
I must somehow make contact with the crew of the Deucalion.

104
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:36,120
But, m'lady, there is one knight we know to be on your side.

105
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,620
The knight who brought you the message from Inaho Kaisuka.

106
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:46,480
Count Mazurek.

107
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:51,580
Now I can demonstrate my loyalty to Her Highness, Princess Asalem.

108
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:54,040
Landing castle, lift off!

109
00:06:54,040 --> 00:07:15,820
Lysdale leader to all units.

110
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:17,960
Take the targets off the starboard bow.

111
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,940
Don't let them get close to the Deucalion.

112
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:22,140
Enemy formation closing 3 o'clock.

113
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:23,560
6-0 elevation angle.

114
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:25,600
Increase starboard AA cannon fire.

115
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:26,960
Dispatch from headquarters.

116
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,560
Orders to withdraw, captain.

117
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,380
Draw now?

118
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:32,040
I guess they must have gotten the results they were after.

119
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,040
Results, ma'am?

120
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:36,220
The real operation that we were only decoys for.

121
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:38,280
Prepare to withdraw.

122
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:40,180
All units return to base.

123
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:43,200
Ma'am, most tanks 0-0 and 1-1 are closing in.

124
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,680
On course for return.

125
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:46,460
Ingo, Inaho made it back.

126
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:47,560
They're cleared for docking.

127
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:48,960
Get them on board ASAP.

128
00:07:48,960 --> 00:08:14,200
That was easy.

129
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:15,640
Seems they were no match for us.

130
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:16,320
Too easy.

131
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:17,260
What are they up to?

132
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:22,880
Count Troiard, the UFE is withdrawing from the battle.

133
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,000
Shall we pursue?

134
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:25,840
No.

135
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:27,700
All units return to base.

136
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,640
They will rearm for the next offensive.

137
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:34,380
Also, I want my landing castle brought in to defend the moon base.

138
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:35,640
Yes, my lord.

139
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:44,580
Is that something that belonged to my sister?

140
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,160
Princess Lemrina.

141
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,700
Did she escape?

142
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:54,520
So, will I ever see her again?

143
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:55,260
Yes.

144
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,760
That you can count on.

145
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:57,380
I do feel...

146
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:00,140
I do feel...

147
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:02,620
Sorry for her.

148
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,080
And for you.

149
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:12,720
Inaho.

150
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:15,720
What is young Kaizuka's condition?

151
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,800
Nothing life-threatening at this point.

152
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:22,900
But still, his cranial nerves are under quite a strain from the analytical engine.

153
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:27,580
I told him not to, but you can see how much he's let its domain expand.

154
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,020
What does that mean, doctor?

155
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:32,020
Inaho has given the machine a part of his brain.

156
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:34,460
Damn crazy kid.

157
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:46,020
I need some way that I can bring this war to an end.

158
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:49,300
I will directly address all of the Orbital Knights.

159
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:52,460
With all due respect, that would not prove sufficient.

160
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:53,660
Why would you say that?

161
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:59,460
From the beginning of hostilities decades ago, the Orbital Knights have been waiting to take the Earth.

162
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:04,580
With that false royal proclamation, Count Troyard has given them a license to do so.

163
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:10,680
He has unified them with promises of great status in the New Kingdom, as well as Alt-Noah activation.

164
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:16,400
But the strongest factor was that announcement of betrothal to you.

165
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:21,180
You would have no credibility if you simply said to end it now.

166
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:25,020
As long as your sister is at his side pretending to be you.

167
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:35,980
Oh, Princess Isalem, it is wonderful to see you looking so well.

168
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:37,460
Thank you for your assistance.

169
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:39,040
It is so kind of you.

170
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,760
More credit than I deserve.

171
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:45,680
Though I must say, your highness, I am relieved at being able to repay my debt.

172
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:46,500
Your debt?

173
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:47,280
Yes.

174
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:49,860
To the Terran boy.

175
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:52,080
Inaho Kaizuka.

176
00:10:52,080 --> 00:11:03,260
I've seen reports that a part of your force went to the moon base.

177
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:06,040
Would you mind explaining why, Captain Mogbarich?

178
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,460
Game time call, sir.

179
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:13,220
If we were to lose the princess now, we would also lose any chance at peace permanently.

180
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,800
What are you saying, Captain?

181
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:19,900
The voice and face of the enemy is not the real Princess Isalem.

182
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,360
We have no evidence whatsoever for that.

183
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,560
Which does not change the truth, sir.

184
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:29,460
We have confirmed the launch of Mazurek Castle.

185
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:36,020
It is said that right before Count Mazurek escaped and fled, he was visited by one of your crew.

186
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:38,100
Yes, that is correct, sir.

187
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:39,060
And your point?

188
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:41,680
Once again, one of your troops was in the area.

189
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:43,760
What a coincidence.

190
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,560
Quite remarkable, indeed.

191
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:51,140
Soon, the Earth and the Moon will be in proximity again.

192
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:56,060
The landing castle stationed on the satellite belt will reinforce moon base defenses.

193
00:11:56,820 --> 00:11:59,660
We need to set a few things straight before that happens.

194
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:03,500
So I will now give you a new mission.

195
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:07,800
We will gather our combined forces and launch an all-out attack on the moon base.

196
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:10,400
The Deucalion will spearhead the attack.

197
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,980
Yes, sir.

198
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,120
I will relay details later.

199
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:16,720
Good luck, Captain.

200
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:21,600
He hates us more than anyone could.

201
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:22,720
Not possible.

202
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:27,500
Because I'm the one who hates him even more.

203
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:31,280
Why would Slane start a war?

204
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:33,680
And bring such destruction?

205
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:34,840
Oh, m'lady.

206
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:38,200
The Slane I knew was so kind.

207
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:39,960
Adored nature.

208
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,920
He truly loved the Earth.

209
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,940
The wondrous things he found there.

210
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:49,620
He was not someone who entertained such pointless conflict.

211
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,160
How could he have done this?

212
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:58,940
Your Highness, Lord Slane has not changed at all deep down.

213
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:03,840
I do not know if the things Lord Slane has done are right or wrong.

214
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:08,580
But he has always cared deeply for you and kept you alive in his heart.

215
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:12,740
He has only wanted whatever it was that would be best for you,

216
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:15,360
even if he thought it might jeopardize his life.

217
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:23,620
And always believing that you would awaken one day.

218
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:29,740
Yes, I have seen that.

219
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,900
Thank you for reminding me, Adel Ritzo.

220
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:40,940
So will you be able to make contact with Verse?

221
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:41,720
Yes.

222
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:45,180
However, understand that His Majesty may be...

223
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:47,520
We cannot afford to stop at half measures now.

224
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:51,580
My Lord Clonkane, I now require your assistance.

225
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,760
I need to use your ship's audience chamber.

226
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,760
Yes, Princess Asalem.

227
00:13:58,200 --> 00:13:59,360
It shall be as you say.

228
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:01,860
Attention all forces.

229
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:05,440
Operations scheduled to commence at 1500 hours UTC.

230
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Man battle stations.

231
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,060
Stand by.

232
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:16,400
Lieutenant Marito.

233
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,420
Headed off to battle, huh?

234
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:20,540
Well, yeah.

235
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:23,260
I'd hope to not go back with you again, Doc.

236
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:26,020
I'm sorry we didn't get the chance.

237
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,560
That doesn't sound like you.

238
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:31,880
Well, it's a low-pressure environment, and I don't want to make myself sick.

239
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,800
No, I didn't mean that.

240
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,320
This won't be our last chance.

241
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:41,560
Yeah, when I'm back.

242
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:46,540
So, this is one of those final showdown kind of deals?

243
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:47,440
I guess so.

244
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,420
If we finish him off, wouldn't it be?

245
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:53,520
If somebody dies in action, I'd call that final, wouldn't you?

246
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:54,540
Hey!

247
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:55,740
Come on, man.

248
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:56,900
Don't jinx us, okay?

249
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,840
Yeah, he's right, you know.

250
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:01,180
All of us are gonna make it back in one piece.

251
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:03,180
My lord slain.

252
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:05,500
The UFE has begun to mass its forces.

253
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,020
How shall we proceed?

254
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,260
As usual.

255
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:11,660
We launch all forces and we intercept the UFE.

256
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:16,580
And in the meantime, we request assistance from the Orbital Knights who back us.

257
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:17,720
Assistant, sir?

258
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,700
This offensive is for the entire Earth.

259
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:26,700
Now the Terrans will know how it feels to have no home to return to.

260
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:33,800
Now!

261
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,640
Oh, Yuki.

262
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,960
Now, do you feel okay?

263
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:42,580
Yeah.

264
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:44,980
I'm so glad.

265
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:47,520
You did really good today.

266
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:48,940
Take it easy for a while.

267
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:54,040
He's going to attack.

268
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:55,220
Everything.

269
00:15:57,440 --> 00:16:00,080
Is it almost time for the mission?

270
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,720
Stay in bed.

271
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:03,900
Don't even think about going anywhere.

272
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:04,960
I'm sorry, Yuki.

273
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:08,320
Something's come up that I have to take care of.

274
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:09,700
You can't now!

275
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:11,020
Yuki, please.

276
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:12,700
Let me go.

277
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:20,080
There's the face that says no matter what, you're going.

278
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:21,900
And you know what else?

279
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:25,340
Here's the voice that says I'm stubborn, so just give in.

280
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:26,720
Damn it, all right.

281
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:30,420
But when you return, we'll have dinner together.

282
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:32,800
That's a death sentence if I ever heard one.

283
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:34,240
Hey, you!

284
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:36,000
You're not allowed to talk like that.

285
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:41,040
You come back alive, and that's a big sister order.

286
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:44,960
You too, Yuki.

287
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:52,680
Hey, Naho.

288
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:54,740
You feeling a little better now?

289
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:57,260
Is this it?

290
00:16:58,140 --> 00:16:58,740
Oh, yeah.

291
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:01,820
The Sleipnir Final Showdown custom job.

292
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:05,360
Sure you don't think that payload's a bit much?

293
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:10,240
Getting close enough to use this stuff in a space battle, you'd have to be nuts.

294
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,660
Looks like things are going to get a little nuts.

295
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:13,880
What do you mean by that?

296
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:15,440
He's not taking this seriously.

297
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:17,460
Inko.

298
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:20,760
Why is it boys always have to be this way?

299
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:24,720
Hey, Naho, you're in no condition to go into battle, and you know it.

300
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:26,780
Why don't you let us handle this one?

301
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:27,680
Because I can't.

302
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,480
Well, why not?

303
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:32,900
Do you think you're some kind of hotshot ace and no one else is as special as you?

304
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:36,000
I promise you, I've never thought about myself that way.

305
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,200
Darn it, Naho!

306
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:39,960
Why can't you just understand?

307
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:43,900
Go out this time, and there's a good chance you won't make it back again.

308
00:17:45,620 --> 00:17:46,580
Please, Naho.

309
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:50,040
We may not have another miracle again like last time.

310
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:52,540
I don't want to.

311
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:56,580
I can't come through that again.

312
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,200
I can't just stay here and do nothing.

313
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:01,080
Hey, he's right, Inko.

314
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:04,720
The kindest thing we could do right now is just say nothing and see him off.

315
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:08,140
I think we ought to be worrying about ourselves right about now.

316
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:10,180
Come on, we gotta face it.

317
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:13,840
Compared to Inaho, our odds of survival are probably lower.

318
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:15,280
Oh, get real!

319
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:17,420
It just so happens I'm an ace too!

320
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:19,440
Huh?

321
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:23,260
I appreciate you both.

322
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:23,940
Thank you.

323
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:25,400
Don't worry.

324
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,060
Everyone will make it back.

325
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:31,340
That's what my left eye tells me.

326
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:34,440
Master switch on.

327
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,220
Fuel cell batteries heating.

328
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:37,780
Confirm voltage.

329
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:38,900
Pump is on.

330
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,360
Accumulator.

331
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,320
Pressure check.

332
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:44,100
Force feedback checking program.

333
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,160
Initiate.

334
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:48,080
Ejection seat functional.

335
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,020
IFF confirmed.

336
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,460
Tactical data link activated.

337
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,280
All systems green.

338
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:56,020
Mustang Zero-Zero.

339
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:57,640
Ready.

340
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:02,140
Hello, Grandfather.

341
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,200
Grandfather.

342
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:07,620
Grandfather, it is I.

343
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:09,100
It is a Salem.

344
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:10,960
Do you recognize me?

345
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:14,740
Oh, a Salem.

346
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:17,020
You look well.

347
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,480
I am quite weary.

348
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:25,540
How are things going for you with our subjugation of the Earth?

349
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:29,000
I have come to you today to ask a favor regarding that.

350
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,440
I would like you to declare a truce with the Earth.

351
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:41,840
Please issue an order commanding the Orbital Knights to immediately cease combat.

352
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,020
I cannot.

353
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:46,700
I will not.

354
00:19:47,180 --> 00:19:48,540
But, Grandfather, why?

355
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:52,440
Earth can never be forgiven.

356
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,560
Do not let up on the attack.

357
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:58,800
Bring that world under our rule.

358
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:06,280
Grandfather, why is it that you hate the Earth so?

359
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,600
Kill Zaria, where is he?

360
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:14,480
Tell me, what has become of my son?

361
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:16,640
Conquer the Earth.

362
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:18,880
Conquer it without delay.

363
00:20:19,540 --> 00:20:21,300
Father passed away years ago.

364
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:23,260
During Heaven's fall.

365
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:26,580
Wretched, filthy Terrans.

366
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:27,860
You killed him.

367
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:29,280
You killed my son.

368
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,180
You even killed my granddaughter.

369
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:34,200
Sweet child to Salem.

370
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,620
I am right here.

371
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:36,620
I am here.

372
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:36,900
I am here.

373
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:41,060
Verse.

374
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:45,460
The name the ancients used when speaking of this world.

375
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:49,840
That is the title they gave to the planet Mars.

376
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:51,820
Oh, Grandfather.

377
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:56,040
Rejoice, rejoice, I say.

378
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:59,700
I have discovered a Martian super-science.

379
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:05,520
The ancients used the name Alt-Noah.

380
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:14,560
A magnificent tool to help mankind make even greater strides.

381
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:22,960
You see, Alt-Noah, is the technology we dreamed of, bringing happiness to mankind.

382
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:25,060
Yes.

383
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:29,280
It is a great power.

384
00:21:30,260 --> 00:21:32,920
It must not ever be misused.

385
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:35,760
Nurture it with care.

386
00:21:36,780 --> 00:21:37,360
I will.

387
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:42,680
Why, who is that standing there?

388
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:44,020
Is that a Salem?

389
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:47,800
How you have grown, my child.

390
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:52,420
You've grown beautiful.

391
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,060
You'll make a wonderful princess.

392
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:01,900
Lead our people to a happy and prosperous future.

393
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:05,680
Yes.

394
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:18,140
Cloncain.

395
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:21,260
I require your resources at my disposal.

396
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:23,220
Your position and connections.

397
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:24,360
Yes.

398
00:22:24,820 --> 00:22:25,820
Of course, gladly.

399
00:22:25,820 --> 00:22:28,240
I thank you for your loyalty.

400
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,120
Count Kruteo.

401
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:34,420
Come and die, you Martian bastard!

402
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:38,700
Glory to first!

403
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:47,240
What the hell is that?

404
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:49,020
Slice them all!

405
00:22:49,020 --> 00:23:01,720
Go, my servants!

406
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:03,140
Wipe them out!

407
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:05,960
Open all channels.

408
00:23:06,260 --> 00:23:08,340
I wish to address every Orbital Knight.

409
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:09,340
Yes, my lord.

410
00:23:09,340 --> 00:23:12,120
Hear my words.

411
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:14,820
The final all-out battle for Earth has begun.

412
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:19,540
Attention, all Orbital Knights in the satellite belt and down on the surface.

413
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:24,100
Launch your attacks against the UFV from all locations at once.

414
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:32,340
This is now the time to demonstrate our vast power to the Terrans once again and show all the UFV the resistance in-

415
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:34,680
Attention, Orbital Knights.

416
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:38,080
Princess Asalem.

417
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:41,700
I am the first and rightful princess of the Empire of Verse.

418
00:23:42,180 --> 00:23:43,760
Asalem vs. Ellusia.

419
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:50,780
This conflict began with but a single spark and has grown into a massive and terrible war.

420
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:52,560
Listen to that.

421
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:54,640
Another pirate broadcast?

422
00:23:55,140 --> 00:23:56,920
Being transmitted on all bands, Captain.

423
00:23:57,300 --> 00:23:57,680
Mm-hmm.

424
00:23:59,100 --> 00:24:04,620
The conflicting hopes and dreams of many different people have resulted in a great tragedy.

425
00:24:06,040 --> 00:24:08,980
This is so sad and awful for everyone.

426
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:20,660
In addition to my grief over this war, I feel both shame and a deep regret over our use of power, for which mankind was not ready.

427
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:24,660
And so, I hereby...

428
00:24:30,660 --> 00:24:38,060
...declare my succession to the Imperial Throne and take my place as Empress of the Verse Empire.

429
00:24:38,980 --> 00:24:45,300
And also, I will be taking as my lawful husband, Count Cruteo of the Orbital Knights.

430
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:51,080
And as the Imperial Family of Verse, we wish to make peace with Earth.

431
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:53,320
You're next time.

432
00:24:55,880 --> 00:25:08,460
nika

433
00:25:08,460 --> 00:25:10,940
you

434
00:25:10,940 --> 00:25:12,160
ゆ

435
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:42,140
See you next time.

436
00:25:42,160 --> 00:26:12,140
See you next time.

437
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:42,140
See you next time.

